## Authentication with a custom provider

You can also use a custom provider to authenticate users. For example, you may want to integrate with an existing authentication system that uses OAuth or OpenID Connect. To do this, you'll need to implement the `AuthProvider` interface and pass it as a prop to the `SignInForm`.

```tsx
// app/auth-provider.ts
import { AuthProvider } from 'aws-amplify'

export class CustomAuthProvider implements AuthProvider  {
  signIn(username: string, password: string): Promise<void> {
    // Implement your custom authentication logic here.
    return new Promise((resolve) => resolve())
  }

  signOut(): void {}
}
```

