## Page Layouts

Page layouts are a way of organizing your pages into sections that make sense.
For example, you might have a layout that looks like this:

- Header
- Sidebar
- Content
- Footer

You can create a page layout by creating a new file in the `app/dashboard` folder.
The filename should be the name of your layout with an `@` prefix and a `.tsx` extension. For example, if you want to create a layout called `Sidebar`, then you would create a file named `app/dashboard/@sidebar.tsx`.

```tsx title="app/dashboard/@sidebar.tsx"
// app/dashboard/@sidebar.tsx
export default function Sidebar() {
  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Sidebar</h1>

      <p>This is the sidebar.</p>
    </div>
  );
}
```

You can then use this layout in your page by importing it and passing it as a prop to `Page`. For example, you could import `@sidebar` into `app/dashboard/@analytics.tsx`:

```tsx title="app/dashboard/@analytics.tsx"
// app/dashboard/@analytics.tsx
import Sidebar from '@dashboard/@sidebar';

export default function Analytics() {
  return (
    <Page layout={Sidebar}>
      <h1>Analytics</h1>

      <p>This is the analytics page.</p>
    </Page>
  );
}
```

