## Page Assertions

Playwright comes with a set of assertions that you can use in your tests. These are available on the `page` object and are documented [here](https://playwright.dev/docs/api/class-pageassertions).

```js
import { test, expect  } from '@playwright/test'

test('homepage loads with main heading', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/')

  // Assert that the main heading is present and contains 'Playwright'.
  const mainHeading = await page.$eval('#main-heading', el => el.textContent)
  expect(mainHeading).toBe('Welcome to the Playwright Test Runner')
})
